Retain attribution and indicate modifications when sharing adapted material.
See SOURCES.md in this directory for attribution, adaptation boundaries and the
source revisions. The notices below apply to the material named; the rest of the
guidance is original.

The beat-sheet and signature-moves study method, the three-part video hook with
its segment, motivation and format matrix, the scene structure of the demo
script, and the content-atoms, testing and caption-tell guidance adapt Corey
Haines' MIT-licensed marketingskills (video, ad-creative, sales-enablement and
social skills). The shared offer brief (audience, trigger and persona framing,
objections, switching forces and buyer language) adapts its product-marketing
skill. Retain the upstream MIT copyright and permission notice in:
licenses/coreyhaines-marketingskills.txt

The social-channel guidance (profile as a promise, content intent by buyer
stage, search, cadence and cross-posting) adapts, with corrections recorded in
SOURCES.md, Pedro Nauck's MIT-licensed insta-master skill. Retain the upstream
MIT copyright and permission notice in:
licenses/pedronauck-skills.txt

The HyperFrames handoff (storyboard format, vertical safe band, caption group
sizes, render-purity rules and CLI behavior) describes HyperFrames by HeyGen,
Inc., licensed under the Apache License 2.0. This skill states facts about the
tool and its documented conventions in its own words and bundles no HyperFrames
code. The license text is kept in:
licenses/heygen-hyperframes.txt
The repository has no NOTICE file at the recorded commit. The guidance here was
changed from the upstream documentation: condensed, reordered, and combined with
this skill's safety defaults.

The shared offer brief also adapts the ICP definition and deal-value skills in
mbfinotti's MIT-licensed sales-skills (account fit separated from persona and
trigger, the hypothesis rule below about 50 closed deals, and provenance labels
for numbers), and Anthropic's Apache-2.0 knowledge-work-plugins create-an-asset
skill (approved sources only, an audience gate and no invented metrics). Retain
the upstream notices in:
licenses/mbfinotti-sales-skills.txt
licenses/anthropic-knowledge-work-plugins.txt
The Apache-2.0 material was changed: rewritten in this skill's own words and
reduced to the rules named here.

Design references that contributed an idea but whose text was not copied, and
that are credited in SOURCES.md without a bundled notice: the edit-list idea
credited to affaan-m/ecc (MIT, not read directly) and the consent-first reply
rule credited to social-media-skills (MIT).
